1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,520
In one Akan tale,

2
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:04,760
all the world’s stories belonged to Nyame,

3
00:00:05,140 --> 00:00:06,060
the sky god.

4
00:00:06,760 --> 00:00:08,820
The spider Anansi wanted to bring them

5
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:09,880
down to the people.

6
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:14,000
Nyame demanded extraordinarily difficult prizes.

7
00:00:14,780 --> 00:00:17,840
Among them were dangerous creatures no small

8
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:19,920
spider should have been able to capture.

9
00:00:21,020 --> 00:00:23,880
Anansi tricked a great python by persuading

10
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:25,840
it to lie against a long stick

11
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:29,180
for measurement. The comparison became a trap.

12
00:00:30,340 --> 00:00:32,740
He deceived hornets with a story about

13
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:35,360
rain and coaxed them into a container.

14
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:39,120
His greatest resource was not size but

15
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:39,940
inventiveness.

16
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,920
By one clever stratagem after another,

17
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,080
Anansi assembled the price.

18
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,820
The sky god had to honor the

19
00:00:48,820 --> 00:00:50,279
